---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero container">
    <p class="kicker">An Open-Source Agentic Gaming Studio</p>
    <h1>Fourth Wall Gaming</h1>
    <div class="divider">✦</div>
    <p class="tagline">
      AI gamemasters, worlds, art, and stories — built on the
      <strong>Mythras</strong> and <strong>Classic Fantasy</strong> ORC rules.
    </p>
    <p class="flavor">
      A table where the gamesmaster never forgets a wound, a debt, or a name.
      You speak; the world answers. The dice are honest, and the ledger is kept.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#campaigns">The three campaigns</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/prez/world-model-with-a-voice/">Read the talk</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The talk, first: it is the clearest single explanation of what this is. -->
  <section class="container talk-section">
    <div class="card talk">
      <p class="kicker-sm">The Talk · LLM-Day San Francisco · 1 October 2026</p>
      <h2>Claude Opus as a Tabletop Roleplaying Gamesmaster</h2>
      <p>
        What it takes to run Mythras Imperative inside a language model, and why a model on its own
        will not do it: a universal rules engine that rolls honestly, a living world of NPC agendas
        on clocks that turn whether or not you are watching, and an epistemics layer where what each
        character knows is a projection from one shared source of truth.
      </p>
      <p class="talk-links">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/prez/world-model-with-a-voice/">Read the slides</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/prez/world-model-with-a-voice/world-model-with-a-voice.pdf">PDF, 25 pages</a>
      </p>
      <p class="small-note">
        The slides are live — arrow keys move through them, and one of them replays a real scene of
        play, typed out at the speed it happened at the table.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider">⚔</div>

  <section class="container" id="campaigns">
    <h2>Three Campaigns</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Three different answers to what an AI gamesmaster is for — a proof, a full game, and a way in
      for somebody who has never played one. All three run on the same engine and the same honest
      dice.
    </p>
    <div class="grid-3 campaigns">

      <article class="card camp accent-cobalt">
        <p class="camp-status">Early demo</p>
        <h3>The Veilwrack: The Stilling</h3>
        <p class="camp-what">An original sky realm</p>
        <p>
          There is no ground. The winged Alar live on the calcified husks of dead sky-leviathans
          above a toxic mist, and this season Lanternfall's windlane began to still. Nobody has
          said the word out loud yet.
        </p>
        <p class="camp-stat">4 spires · 7 factions · 46 lore entries · a five-act arc</p>
        <p class="camp-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/fourth-wall-gaming/veilwrack-campaign">The worldbook →</a>
          <a href="/craft/">How it was made →</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="card camp accent-ruby">
        <p class="camp-status">The full game</p>
        <h3>And Then the Dragons Came: Purewater</h3>
        <p class="camp-what">Classic Fantasy, for players who know the form</p>
        <p>
          A canal city where the Lake Lady's holy water meets the sea, three days before a sacred
          tourney. A baron has arrived with a champion nobody is allowed to see. Four strangers
          turn up the same week.
        </p>
        <p class="camp-stat">4 entry points · 42 characters · 15 agendas on clocks</p>
        <p class="camp-links">
          <a href="https://fourth-wall-gaming.github.io/purewater-campaign/">Both guidebooks →</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/fourth-wall-gaming/purewater-campaign">The repo →</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="card camp accent-emerald">
        <p class="camp-status">A first roleplaying game</p>
        <h3>First Through</h3>
        <p class="camp-what">Science fiction, written for ten- to fifteen-year-olds</p>
        <p>
          The doors between stars are instant, and only the young can use them, so the entire
          traffic of human space rides on fifteen-year-olds. Every star, distance and planet in it
          is a real and current measurement.
        </p>
        <p class="camp-stat">Build your own character · Act One is one sitting · a page for parents</p>
        <p class="camp-links">
          <a href="https://fourth-wall-gaming.github.io/first-through-campaign/">Both guidebooks →</a>
          <a href="https://fourth-wall-gaming.github.io/first-through-campaign/for-parents.html">For parents →</a>
        </p>
      </article>

    </div>
    <p class="campaigns-foot">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/play/">Install one and open the first scene</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="divider">✦</div>

  <section class="container">
    <div class="rules-box card">
      <p class="rules-head">How a check resolves at this table</p>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="die">d100</td><td>Roll under your skill. The difficulty grade — <em>Easy</em> to <em>Herculean</em> — is declared before the dice fall.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="die">⚔</td><td>Combat runs the full Mythras exchange: differential rolls, special effects, hit locations, armour, wounds.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="die">✦</td><td>Every roll is returned as auditable JSON. The gamesmaster <strong>cannot</strong> fudge.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The Workshop</h2>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Mythras GM</h3>
        <p>The engine the three campaigns run on. A deterministic d100 rules engine, combat
        resolution, character generation and campaign publishing, all persisted in TypeDB —
        so you can walk away mid-scene and come back weeks later.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/fourth-wall-gaming/mythras-gm">The engine, on GitHub →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-amber">
        <h3>Behind the Screen</h3>
        <p>How it works: the rules engine that cannot be talked out of a result, a knowledge
        graph as the save file, and campaigns published as Git repos.</p>
        <a href="/tech/">The architecture →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Gallery</h3>
        <p>What the games left behind — novels written out of real played sessions, with the
        dialogue taken from the transcript, and art generated alongside the worlds.</p>
        <a href="/gallery/">Browse the gallery →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mythras-plug">
    <div class="card accent-emerald">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0; border-bottom:none">Built on Mythras — Get the Real Game</h2>
      <p>Everything here runs on the <em>Mythras Imperative</em> SRD under the ORC License.
      Mythras is one of the finest d100 systems ever written: fast, deadly, deeply
      simulationist. If you enjoy playing it with an AI gamemaster, buy the books and
      play it with your friends.</p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://thedesignmechanism.com">The Design Mechanism</a> publishes
        <em>Mythras</em>, <em>Mythras Imperative</em>, and <em>Classic Fantasy</em>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero { text-align: center; padding: 3.5rem 1.25rem 1rem; }
    .kicker {
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.22em;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }
    .hero h1 { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; }
    .hero .divider { margin: 1.25rem auto; max-width: 18rem; }
    .tagline {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--text);
      max-width: 38rem;
      margin: 0 auto 1rem;
    }
    .flavor {
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      max-width: 34rem;
      margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    }
    .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.9rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    section.container { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .rules-box { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; }
    .rules-head {
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      font-weight: 700;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule);
      padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }
    .rules-box table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
    .rules-box td { padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem 0.45rem 0; vertical-align: top; color: var(--text-dim); }
    .rules-box td.die {
      font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--ruby);
      white-space: nowrap;
      width: 3.5rem;
    }
    .mythras-plug { margin-top: 1rem; }
    .talk { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; }
    .talk h2 { margin: 0.2rem 0 0.75rem; border-bottom: none; }
    .kicker-sm {
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .talk p { color: var(--text-dim); }
    .talk-links { display: flex; gap: 0.9rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 1.25rem 0 0; }
    .small-note { font-size: 0.875rem; font-style: italic; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
    .section-lede { color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
    .camp { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; }
    .camp h3 { margin: 0.1rem 0 0.15rem; }
    .camp-status {
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--ruby);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .camp.accent-cobalt .camp-status { color: var(--cobalt); }
    .camp.accent-emerald .camp-status { color: var(--emerald); }
    .camp-what { font-style: italic; color: var(--text-dim); margin: 0 0 0.7rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .camp-stat {
      font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .camp-stat { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 0.6rem; }
    .camp-links { margin: 0.9rem 0 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; }
    .camp-links a { font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .campaigns-foot { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  </style>
</Base>
